# RelayFirst — ignore rules

# Go
/bin/
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Node / TypeScript
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Foundry build artifacts (S7). `forge build` writes compiled output here; it is
# derived from contracts/ and must not be committed or copied into an image.
out/
cache/
broadcast/

# Secrets — CODING_RULES.md §8
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# Local data / scratch
/data/
/tmp/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.db

# KAT corpus is generated but IS committed on purpose: it is the cross-language
# contract (CODING_RULES.md §4). Do not add testdata/ here.
!testdata/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Tool scaffolding that initialises itself inside a repository.
#
# `relayfirst/` and `relayfirst-sdd/` appeared during a session without anyone creating them: they
# hold only spec-kit scaffolding (.specify/, .github/skills/speckit-*/) and no project code. They
# were briefly staged and then unstaged, which is exactly how such a directory ends up committed —
# `git add -A` does not distinguish "this is mine" from "a tool left this here".
#
# They are ignored rather than deleted so that a tool relying on them keeps working, and so that
# removing them stays a separate decision from forgetting them.
/relayfirst/
/relayfirst-sdd/
